@Honny1 yes, sorry about that. The squashed commit had the new message but the code change never made it into the push. I've pushed it now in 5ae9ed9 as a separate commit on top. The error is now:

`unsupported transport "docker" for looking up local images: "docker://quay.io/foo/bar" is not a local image name`

I ran `gofmt` and `go vet` on `libimage`. I can squash the two commits if you'd like.
